# Git Branch & Commit Workflow

## Branch Model
- `main`: Always stable and usable with no major bugs. Never commit directly to `main`; only merge verified `dev` states into `main`.
- `dev`: Integration branch. All feature and bugfix branches start from `dev` and merge back into `dev`.
- `feature/<name>`: Used for new features or milestone tasks (e.g. `feature/m4-packaging`).
- `bugfix/<name>`: Used for bug fixes (e.g. `bugfix/refresh-restore`).
- Flow: `feature/*` or `bugfix/*` -> `dev` -> `main`.

## Commit Message Convention
Every commit subject must start with a lowercase type prefix:
- `feature: <summary>` — new features, capabilities, or user-facing improvements
- `bugfix: <summary>` — bug fixes and regressions
- `chore: <summary>` — build scripts, CI, docs, refactors, or tooling

## Hygiene & Security
- Never commit `.env`, Plex tokens, local machine paths, personal server names/IPs/ports, or debug logs.
- Only commit when requested by the user.
